            <ArticleTitle>Asthma associated with exercise.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>31-43</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Exercise is a potent stimulus to asthma. The diagnosis is not always straightforward, and health care providers should have a high index of suspicion. Treatment usually controls exercise-induced asthma but usually requires therapy tailored for each individual patient.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
